So for any application we need to really evaluate what these models offer relative to the current baselines.

193
00:24:46,149 --> 00:24:53,029
Now the benefits could be in the form of the improved time to solve, improved quality,

194
00:24:53,029 --> 00:24:57,909
a reduction in cost or new capabilities that were not possible before.

195
00:24:57,909 --> 00:25:02,630
Now this evaluation is critical because if we don't do it, we might end up with poor choices.

196
00:25:02,630 --> 00:25:12,710
Now broadly speaking, there are three groups of applications where gen models turn out to be a poor fit when we do this evaluation of benefits.

197
00:25:12,710 --> 00:25:15,909
And let me call out these three groups.

198
00:25:15,909 --> 00:25:22,870
The first one is applications that do not involve understanding or generation over unstructured input like text and images.

199
00:25:22,880 --> 00:25:29,350
And obviously because the models forte is this unstructured input.

200
00:25:29,350 --> 00:25:34,470
So if we are not dealing with it maybe we don't need them as much.

201
00:25:34,470 --> 00:25:42,710
And examples here include inventory optimization or structured predictive analytics based on tabular numeric data.

202
00:25:42,710 --> 00:25:54,630
Now the second group includes high stakes applications which are centered around understanding but not generation of unstructured inputs and this could be like fraud detection, medical diagnosis.

203
00:25:54,630 --> 00:26:08,549
Here we are still dealing with unstructured inputs but we are only understanding and the accuracy bar is really high and usually for such task we also have a lot of task specific label data.

204
00:26:08,549 --> 00:26:20,310
So it's better to train highly accurate and controllable encoder models that can be efficiently retrained as new data keeps coming in than go to generative models.

205
00:26:20,310 --> 00:26:27,430
Now the third group includes realtime high volume low latency systems like transaction scoring

206
00:26:27,440 --> 00:26:40,390
or e-commerce product search ranking where the computational cost and the inherent latency of generative models just makes them impractical for production use.

207
00:26:40,390 --> 00:26:45,269
Yeah, I mean now of course I can go into more detail but these are the three broad buckets.

208
00:26:45,269 --> 00:26:47,909
If I were to summarize this,

209
00:26:47,909 --> 00:26:54,789
if you needed an application with a lot of accuracy and it has already been worked on

210
00:26:54,789 --> 00:27:06,549
with pre-existing modeling and an solution exists, then don't go and use generative AI in these cases cuz it would not make sense.

