00:53:33,359 --> 00:53:38,069
Yeah, there are few special kinds of tools that are worth mentioning.

422
00:53:38,069 --> 00:53:40,710
The first one is a retriever tool.

423
00:53:40,710 --> 00:53:50,151
Sometimes people refer to it as a knowledge access tool and this is equivalent to a research analyst who goes and fetches information. Right?

424
00:53:50,151 --> 00:53:54,630
We already saw that retrieval augmented generation that's RAD.

425
00:53:54,630 --> 00:54:08,230
There is a specialized retriever tool that goes and fetches information from databases or some external repositories and that enables the agent to have access to factual information and you know grounds it.

426
00:54:08,230 --> 00:54:13,510
The second one which is again very important is a safety or guardrails tools.

427
00:54:13,510 --> 00:54:27,670
Sometimes this is actually implemented across different layers as separate tools but essentially it plays a role of a compliance or you know quality assurance officer.

428
00:54:27,670 --> 00:54:32,470
Uh it makes sure that the input is within scope and the output is safe and aligned to the policy guidelines.

429
00:54:32,480 --> 00:54:34,471
Right? So that is the job of this tool.

430
00:54:34,480 --> 00:54:43,829
Now just wanted to call out that you know these tools don't just handle information they can even perform actions like

431
00:54:43,829 --> 00:54:55,750
uh a tool could go and fill a form just like a human would do send emails you know control a mouse or in case of embodied systems it can capture images stuff like that.

432
00:54:55,750 --> 00:55:00,470
So putting it all together, the planner decides what needs to happen.

433
00:55:00,470 --> 00:55:04,150
The orchestrator manages how it happens.

434
00:55:04,150 --> 00:55:07,349
The LLM provides the intelligence.

435
00:55:07,349 --> 00:55:12,150
Memory ensures that there is continuity of the context and the tools do all the specialized work.

436
00:55:12,160 --> 00:55:16,951
And you know this process is also iterative. It's not like a linear flow.

437
00:55:16,960 --> 00:55:22,630
And you know planning, execution, reflection, learning, all of this happens in loops.

438
00:55:22,640 --> 00:55:25,109
Mhm.

