01:00:09,990 --> 01:00:15,349
So the input layer needs to flag anything that is out of scope,

477
01:00:15,349 --> 01:00:21,430
unsafe, malicious upfront and typically we use a mix of deterministic filters like whitelisted phrases,

478
01:00:21,440 --> 01:00:29,349
blacklisted phrases, reax patterns and so on and also some lightweight ML models.

479
01:00:29,349 --> 01:00:38,710
lightweight because we don't want to add to the latency of generation and also because they are more accurate at like flagging anything

480
01:00:38,710 --> 01:00:45,349
that is unsafe and these checks have to be fast right so that's the reason we do this and apart from the input layer

481
01:00:45,349 --> 01:00:54,549
we also have some safeguards in the prompting layer so you can do that by giving instructions to the planner or the LLM core itself

