01:01:05,829 --> 01:01:14,630
it can also give an output field which conveys how confident it is in this response which can be a signal

485
01:01:14,630 --> 01:01:26,230
to the orchestrator and the orchestrator can use that to decide if there's something else that needs to be done maybe another round of verification or just blocking the response.

486
01:01:26,230 --> 01:01:28,630
Now the next layer that comes into play is the output validation.

487
01:01:28,630 --> 01:01:38,789
So in the output validation layer again we have similar to the input validation we have a deterministic sub layer as well as a modeling based one.

488
01:01:38,789 --> 01:01:44,630
The deterministic one will have blacklisted phrases and so on.

489
01:01:44,630 --> 01:01:53,750
And the ML model layer could check for like things like bias, toxicity, factual accuracy, whether it's really entailed and grounded in evidence and so on.

490
01:01:53,750 --> 01:01:56,470
Now in addition to these input validation,

491
01:01:56,480 --> 01:02:05,270
prompting and output validation layers often we also have a human in the loop mechanisms like allowing the users

