01:05:35,510 --> 01:05:37,670
So it's essentially programming through natural language.

524
01:05:37,680 --> 01:05:47,190
And most of what you called out they can just briefly go over those prompting techniques like zeroshot prompting is just a direct instruction.

525
01:05:47,190 --> 01:05:52,069
Few short prompting is one where you give some examples.

526
01:05:52,069 --> 01:05:54,309
It's also called in context learning.

527
01:05:54,309 --> 01:06:02,069
So this is a case where we show a few examples and say you know this is how I would like you to do the job.

528
01:06:02,069 --> 01:06:12,710
And for more complex reasoning we use techniques like chain of thought prompting and where we tell the model to think step by step and we provide examples.

529
01:06:12,710 --> 01:06:15,430
So this is similar to how one might do math problems.

530
01:06:15,430 --> 01:06:19,510
we would do step by step and that reduces chance of error.

531
01:06:19,510 --> 01:06:30,950
Now apart from that there are lot of other variants like self-consistency, tree of thought, graph of thought and here the model explores multiple reasoning paths and it compares and picks the best one.

532
01:06:30,950 --> 01:06:40,230
Chain of verification is another useful one where the prompt instructs the model to generate an answer and then double checks and critics it.

533
01:06:40,230 --> 01:06:48,630
And when the tasks are you know a little bit more complex we often end up hitting context window limits.

534
01:06:48,630 --> 01:06:56,230
So in those cases we actually break it down into multiple parts and use something called prompt chaining.

535
01:06:56,230 --> 01:07:02,309
So essentially the output of one of the earlier prompts will be fed as the input to one of the later prompts.

536
01:07:02,309 --> 01:07:08,710
So if you think of all of these techniques whether it is chain of thought, chain of verification, prompt chaining or prompt decomposition,

537
01:07:08,710 --> 01:07:16,470
these are all very intuitive because that is how we typically solve problems as humans.

538
01:07:16,470 --> 01:07:27,349
Now what I mentioned earlier, the earlier generation of these models, we really had to be very careful in terms of how we communicate with these models mean how we prompt them.

